Z||000000||RobertVol||01-28-2001||02:19 PM||||I want to get a factory sub woofer for my 88gt. Now my question is I have heard that if you have a T top car the fitting is different and you cant use one from a Solid roof car. But when I look at the console fitting on my T top car I see that the fitting is got a hole were the slider will go and it can be removed. Why can I not just removed the console fitting from around the one I purchase and just fit the slider mechanism behind the colsole fitting I have?<P>Thanks,<BR><P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||01-28-2001||02:49 PM||||If I remember correcly that is what you need to do. Remove slider switch from one and install it on the other.||||reg||14
Z||000002||RobertVol||01-28-2001||10:40 PM||||Thanks Oreif! <P>Thats what I was thinking but just thought I would make sure. NOW......<P>To find a good one in good shape that will match the beechwood interior ...hmmmmm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=819451&a=5959473&p=36934984&Sequence=1"> ||||reg||1
